+# Scene panel presentation unit (tentative)
+
+Tags: #scene #panel #particles #palette #unit
+
+Range: 08057960–08059428, end exclusive. All 52 existing functions were
+consolidated in ROM order into `src/scene_panel_presentation.c`. No gaps,
+unmatched functions, new matches, or NONMATCHING drafts were present.
+The range remains 100% matching, a 0.000 percentage-point gain (6,856 bytes
+preserved). Repository matched-code percentage and register-pinned percentage
+are unchanged by the consolidation.
+
+## Shared layout
+
+Reused `include/scene_panel.h` because these consumers use the existing
+`ScenePanel` object. Removed the separate `ScenePanelEffectsView` and
+`ScenePanelScheduleView`; their headers now carry API declarations and include
+the common layout. No other subsystem's object view was reinterpreted.
+
+The shared header now describes the time-palette banks at 0x20, three palette
+sources at 0x220, selectors at 0x22C/0x22D, main sprite at 0x254, particle pool
+at 0x560, time phase at 0xC0B, scheduled-action fields at 0x134C–0x1368,
+action parameter at 0x13C4, palette blend counters at 0x142C/0x142E, and pending
+script ID at 0x17AC. Existing presentation channels, maps, overlay levels,
+origin, center, subject pointers, state and effect counters remain at their
+original offsets. Unknown storage is explicitly retained.
+
+`ScenePanelParticles` contains 32 0x34-byte particle records plus the resource
+pointer and active/cursor bytes. Its natural two-byte tail alignment occupies
+0xBE6–0xBE8, exactly before the existing subject array. Main sprite, graphics,
+script arguments, palette-loop scratch, and packed word-vector helper types
+also live in the shared header. Overlay initialization now uses the same
+`SceneOverlayResource` declaration as the overlay drawer. Interpretations are
+static and tentative; this work adds no runtime coverage claims.
+
+## Matching adaptations and naming
+
+Direct field access replaced the palette-source, palette-buffer, overlay-map,
+and shake-offset casts. Dynamic array byte offsets remain where they index
+palette data. The scheduled-action initializer at 080592F4 retains two small
+runtime-offset adaptations: the interval store derives 0x134E from 0x1364,
+and the null callback store keeps 0x1360 in the original register. Replacing
+both with direct field addresses changed 25 bytes; restoring only the interval
+left three differing bytes. Both adaptations have comments in the unit.
+
+The background effect retains a packed bitfield/word union because its original
+code performs whole-word updates while preserving adjacent halfwords. Sprite
+helper prototypes were unchanged; no engine.h API incompatibility was found.
+
+Existing local aliases are preserved once each: ScenePanel_SetChannelTwo
+(08058168), ScenePanel_SetChannelFive (08058184), and
+ScenePanel_BeginReverseSequence (0805822C). The other functions already have
+published descriptive names. No symbol registry changes were made.
+
+## Verification and process
+
+All 52 individual functions passed after shared-type unification. The merged,
+formatted unit passed tools/check.py with zero differing bytes across the
+entire 6,856-byte range. make format and git diff --check passed.
+tools/progress.py reports unchanged matched bytes and register-pinned bytes.
+
+Ran tools/depin.py --write on the six previously hinted inputs: hint counts
+remained 2, 27, 12, 4, 35, and 2 respectively. No new pins or barriers were
+added. There were roughly 65 deliberate check compilations (individual and
+merged), plus about 88 automated hint-removal trials.
+
+Used tools/merge_unit.py's merge and --write workflow, replacing only its git rm
+operation in memory with ordinary file deletion to honor the driver's explicit
+no-git-metadata instruction. No tools were edited, no commits were made, and
+no shared docs or symbol inventories were edited.
+
+Full combined validation: `build/venv/bin/python tools/build.py` printed
+`build/boktai3.gba: OK`. The first attempt compiled all C but discovered this
+fresh worktree lacked `build/res/` extraction inputs required by shared gen/data.s.
+Copied the existing baseline resource inputs into the worktree's own build/res/
+(no sharing or modification of another build tree), then reran with cached C
+objects. The complete build and ROM comparison passed. Final matched-byte count equaled the baseline (no regression).
